            <h2>Heat Exchanger Analysis &amp; Virtual Lab</h2>

            <p>
                Developed a MATLAB-based virtual laboratory for heat exchanger analysis
                as part of a 2-member team at the DCRUST National-Level Chemical
                Engineering Hackathon – Virtual Lab, where the project received 3rd Prize.
            </p>

            <h3>What I Worked On</h3>

            <ul>
                <li>Developed the complete heat exchanger analysis module, including heat-duty and energy-balance calculations</li>

                <li>Implemented LMTD-based analysis for both parallel-flow and counter-flow configurations</li>

                <li>Studied the effect of hot-fluid flow rate, overall heat-transfer coefficient, and cold-fluid outlet temperature on heat-transfer performance and required area</li>

                <li>Built the analysis in MATLAB to enable systematic comparison of different operating and design conditions</li>

                <li>Presented the virtual-lab solution at the national-level Chemical Engineering hackathon</li>
            </ul>

